 "summary": "The new coefficient-transitivity square and the smooth-restriction preservation lemmas have no existing Tau Ceti or Mathlib counterpart, and the proofs reuse the existing smooth transitivity and pure-tensor rules plus Mathlib's finite-product reindexing (`Fintype.prod_equiv`, `Fintype.prod_prod_type`) rather than re-deriving them. `smoothResFunctor_trivialF2` lifts the TopRep-level `res_trivialF2_hom` to the smooth subtype, has a consumer and is not derivable from `smoothResFunctor_obj` alone.",
